/*!
\page page_sttriggeridcollection StTriggerIdCollection — Collection Documentation

\section tic_overview Overview

\ref StTriggerIdCollection stores the complete set of <b>trigger IDs</b> for a
single event in \ref StEvent.

STAR's trigger system evaluates events at three levels (L1, L2, L3); this class
holds a separate \ref StTriggerId object for each level and for an expanded L3
set, plus a <b>nominal</b> \ref StTriggerId representing the consensus decision.
<b>Most analyses should access only \c nominal()</b>.

Each \ref StTriggerId stores up to 42 trigger IDs that fired, per-trigger version
numbers (name, threshold, prescale), and a 64-bit bitmask.

\section tic_ownership Object Ownership

All five \ref StTriggerId pointers are initialised to \c nullptr in the constructor
and are <b>explicitly deleted in the destructor</b>.  Callers must not delete the
objects returned by the accessors.

| Pointer | Ownership |
|---------|-----------|
| mL1TriggerId | Owned — deleted in destructor. |
| mL2TriggerId | Owned — deleted in destructor. |
| mL3TriggerId | Owned — deleted in destructor. |
| mL3ExpandedTriggerId | Owned — deleted in destructor. |
| mNominalTriggerId | Owned — deleted in destructor. |

The collection itself is owned by the \c StEvent framework.

\section tic_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \ref StTriggerId* | mL1TriggerId | Trigger IDs that passed the L1 (hardware) decision. May be \c nullptr. |
| \ref StTriggerId* | mL2TriggerId | Trigger IDs that passed the L2 decision. May be \c nullptr. |
| \ref StTriggerId* | mL3TriggerId | Trigger IDs that passed the L3 (software) decision. May be \c nullptr. |
| \ref StTriggerId* | mL3ExpandedTriggerId | Extended L3 trigger ID set (Run 6+). May be \c nullptr. |
| \ref StTriggerId* | mNominalTriggerId | <b>Nominal (consensus) trigger IDs — use this for analyses.</b> |

\section tic_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c nominal() const | Returns the nominal \ref StTriggerId. <b>Primary accessor for analyses.</b> |
| \c l1() const | Returns the L1 \ref StTriggerId; may be \c nullptr. |
| \c l2() const | Returns the L2 \ref StTriggerId; may be \c nullptr. |
| \c l3() const | Returns the L3 \ref StTriggerId; may be \c nullptr. |
| \c l3Expanded() const | Returns the expanded L3 \ref StTriggerId; may be \c nullptr. |
| \c setNominal(StTriggerId*) | Assigns nominal; collection takes ownership. |
| \c setL1 / setL2 / setL3 / setL3Expanded | Assign the respective level's object; collection takes ownership. |

\section tic_striggerid StTriggerId Quick Reference

- \c isTrigger(unsigned int id) — \c true if trigger \c id fired.
- \c triggerIds() — \c vector of all fired trigger IDs.
- \c mask() — 64-bit fired-trigger bitmask.
- \c version(id) / \c nameVersion(id) / \c thresholdVersion(id) / \c prescaleVersion(id) — per-trigger versioning.

\section tic_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StTriggerIdCollection* trigColl = event->triggerIdCollection();
if (!trigColl) return;

const StTriggerId* nominal = trigColl->nominal();
if (nominal && nominal->isTrigger(15007)) {
    // event passed trigger 15007
}

if (nominal) {
    vector<unsigned int> ids = nominal->triggerIds();
    for (size_t i = 0; i < ids.size(); ++i) {
        unsigned int id       = ids[i];
        unsigned int prescale = nominal->prescaleVersion(id);
    }
}
\endcode

\see StTriggerId
*/
